00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:13.127
There's next week, and then the week after that is the last episode.

00:00:13.127 --> 00:00:17.060
Originally I'd thought that this was going to be the conclusion of the Ogre story line but that's

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:21.400
spilling over into next week so that's going to be a three part story line with his character.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:26.360
I feel like we were all in agreement this week that the Riddler was probably the redeeming quality of this episode.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:29.920
He's consistently the most fun thing about this show.

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:34.720
Fingers crossed in season two that they spend a little bit more time in each episode with his character.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:38.020
They can do that. They can course correct like that if one character just becomes

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:40.020
vastly more popular than the others.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:41.380
it doesn't always happen because

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:44.400
sometimes they've already made the episodes so it's too late to change.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:49.600
One of the good things about Gotham right now though is they've been picked up for season two so they have another twenty-two episodes

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.639
and they haven't even started writing it yet  so they can look at the characters

00:00:52.639 --> 00:00:54.884
that the audience has been rallying behind and just

00:00:54.884 --> 00:00:57.400
spend more time developing those characters.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.820
So let's just go ahead and get into it. Careful for spoilers from the episode

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:02.475
if you haven't seen it yet. Starting with top five moments.

00:01:02.493 --> 00:01:05.533
Number five: Barbara is captured by the Ogre.

00:01:05.533 --> 00:01:08.273
I don't know if captured is the right word because she did go willingly.

00:01:08.273 --> 00:01:11.835
That's kind of his MO. He just charms them into his sex dungeon.

00:01:11.835 --> 00:01:14.040
It's like Fifty Shades of Gotham right now.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:17.606
I couldn't remember but I feel like the sex dungeon was actually in the promos.

00:01:17.606 --> 00:01:20.131
I feel like that's a promo moment that they would show off. 

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:23.500
There are only a few things that pass through your mind when you see a shot like that. One you think

00:01:23.503 --> 00:01:25.280
Fifty Shades of Grey sex room,

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:28.116
or two you think of Jigsaw with the Saw movies.

00:01:28.116 --> 00:01:31.076
Like classic Texas Chainsaw Massacre type horror. 

00:01:31.076 --> 00:01:36.464
I feel like the crazy torture room would actually be the more preferable option just because Fifty Shades of Grey was such a terrible movie.

00:01:36.464 --> 00:01:41.351
It'd be more fun if they were going for more outright comedy but that's not what they're going for with the Ogre story line. 

00:01:41.351 --> 00:01:43.960
He's meant to be very threatening and very scary

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:47.060
even though he's coming off more like a Tim Burton villain

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:48.443
you know one that you laugh at.

00:01:48.443 --> 00:01:51.160
There are a few exceptions to that. I feel like Danny Devito

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:52.960
balanced the line between funny

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:54.980
and terrifying really really well.

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:58.798
The ogre story line is really the backbone of this theme that's been crossing these

00:01:58.798 --> 00:02:01.058
I guess these three episodes you can call them now. 

00:02:01.058 --> 00:02:03.199
People killing to save those that they love.

00:02:03.199 --> 00:02:07.374
Is Gordon going to kill the Ogre to save Barbara, even though they're estranged?

00:02:07.374 --> 00:02:11.137
Short answer: yes. Even though we don't know if the Ogre is actually going to die.

00:02:11.137 --> 00:02:13.980
We can say he'll probably commit to killing the Ogre

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.976
to save Barbara whether or not it actually ends up going down that way.

00:02:16.976 --> 00:02:19.331
Comic book shows have a way of saving villains like

00:02:19.331 --> 00:02:22.591
they find some out so they could always come back in a future season. 

00:02:22.591 --> 00:02:25.750
What I'm really hoping to see out of this Barbara/Ogre story line 

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:28.802
is like a dramatic character shift in Barbara.

00:02:28.802 --> 00:02:31.838
I haven't felt like her character has been very interesting and I feel like

00:02:31.838 --> 00:02:34.240
they could use this trauma, this Ogre trauma, 

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:37.606
to take the character in a different direction and just have a little bit more fun with her.

00:02:37.606 --> 00:02:42.244
On to number four: Bruce and Selina go on a super special date to try and do some super sleuthing.

00:02:42.244 --> 00:02:44.200
Here's the thing about all the Bruce and Selina stuff:

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:47.655
This was a lot of fun like I really like their moments together but I feel like

00:02:47.655 --> 00:02:50.160
they work better on a show say like The Flash that

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.620
plays more on lighthearted comedy.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:55.100
I feel like children just work better in that context.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:59.553
Unless it's going to be some crazy horror flick and that's not really what Gotham is.

00:02:59.553 --> 00:03:03.236
The thing I really like about Bruce and Selina is that Selina

00:03:03.236 --> 00:03:05.880
is probably the strongest female character on the show

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:07.680
and she's the youngest which is just hilarious.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:12.765
She's kind of the brains of the operation even though Batman becomes the world's greatest detective.

00:03:12.765 --> 00:03:14.382
She's the one that always knows what's up.

00:03:14.382 --> 00:03:18.642
I think she made her feelings for Bruce pretty clear when she pushed Alfred's friend out the window.

00:03:18.642 --> 00:03:21.595
That's kind of like her version of what's going on with the Ogre.

00:03:21.595 --> 00:03:25.853
People crossing the line to save people that they really care about or love.

00:03:25.853 --> 00:03:29.472
I don't think that Catwoman loves Bruce, like their relationship isn't that intense yet.

00:03:29.472 --> 00:03:32.526
Moving on to number three: The Penguin vs Maroni.

00:03:32.526 --> 00:03:35.673
So if you remember the last episode he's just working his way up to just

00:03:35.673 --> 00:03:36.925
getting rid of Maroni

00:03:36.925 --> 00:03:39.975
but we also have Fish Mooney that's coming in from left field too.

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:42.460
We're so close to the finale

00:03:42.531 --> 00:03:45.091
that all of the mob elements of the show

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:48.459
are going to turn on each other and go crazy in a Battle Royale. 

00:03:48.459 --> 00:03:50.807
I feel like the show is just backing the Penguin 

00:03:50.807 --> 00:03:53.020
as the protagonist of this story line.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:55.560
Even though he is one of the more notable batman villains.

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:58.227
I don't think of him as an antagonist on the show.

00:03:58.227 --> 00:04:01.677
The show wants you to root for him so that makes him a protagonist.

00:04:01.677 --> 00:04:06.140
Yes Jada Pinkett Smith did spoil a few things that might be going down in the finale so

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:10.107
let's just not mention them in the comments or if you do please use spoiler tags.

00:04:10.107 --> 00:04:13.359
I feel like if you've been frustrated with the Penguin's story line

00:04:13.359 --> 00:04:15.940
you'll be really happy with what goes down in the finale

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:17.980
like he'll get his really bloody gruesome moment.

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:19.813
He's killed a lot of people this season.

00:04:19.813 --> 00:04:25.360
Arguably I think it was a bigger WTF when we saw the Riddler kill someone because he'd never done it before.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:31.980
Once you do it the first time each subsequent killing becomes less and less of a WTF unless they're killing a character that you love.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:36.423
Most of the people the penguin has killed have been third rate henchmen so it's not that big of a deal.

00:04:36.423 --> 00:04:40.460
You could argue that Maroni was trying to cozy up to his mother

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:44.031
so he's trying to kill someone to protect a woman that he loves

00:04:44.031 --> 00:04:45.772
just like the other characters in the show.

00:04:45.772 --> 00:04:49.329
With the exception of Bruce and Selina where you can flip the gender roles.

00:04:49.329 --> 00:04:53.498
On to number two: Barbara drinks a little bit of the Ogre Kool-Aid. 

00:04:53.498 --> 00:04:56.850
There's a certain part of me that feels like she almost went into that

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:58.600
torture dungeon willingly so

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:00.959
you just wonder what's going through her mind.

00:05:00.959 --> 00:05:02.540
If you've been watching Daredevil

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:04.063
the Vanessa character is like this

00:05:04.063 --> 00:05:07.400
really complex interesting female character that

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:10.080
