00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.220
She enters into this really twisted relationship with the main villain

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:17.320
but she doesn't canonize him. They have a very loving relationship.

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:22.007
So you wonder what is going on inside her head. It's just fascinating to me.

00:05:22.007 --> 00:05:26.480
I feel like this Ogre story line could be a redemption for Barbara's character.

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:29.314
I feel like there's a couple logical ways that it could go down.

00:05:29.314 --> 00:05:30.880
You could play it straight

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:35.000
Gordon saves her and they jump starts their relationship and just try to deal with the trauma.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:38.145
That's like the safety option. I hope they don't go that route.

00:05:38.145 --> 00:05:40.180
The second more interesting option is

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:43.331
that it pushes her over the edge and she goes super dark.

00:05:43.331 --> 00:05:46.880
Originally when they were conceiving the show the Barbara Kean character

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:49.933
was actually a different character. They changed it just a little bit.

00:05:49.933 --> 00:05:52.083
I think she was originally intended to be

00:05:52.083 --> 00:05:54.780
something of a proto Batgirl like

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:58.030
